.* Caribbean Poker Help
:userdoc.

:h1 res=001.General Help
:font facename=Helv size=8x12.
:p.
Caribbean Poker is a casino card game that you play alone against the dealer. It comes in two variants, chosen in the Game menu between hands&colon. :hp2.Stud:ehp2. (as in Caribbean Stud Poker) and :hp2.Draw:ehp2., where you may exchange cards. Choose a topic&colon.
:p.
:ul compact.
:li.:link reftype=hd res=002.How to begin:elink.
:li.:link reftype=hd res=003.Stud:elink.
:li.:link reftype=hd res=004.Draw:elink.
:li.:link reftype=hd res=005.Progressive jackpot:elink.
:li.:link reftype=hd res=006.Payout table:elink.
:li.:link reftype=hd res=007.Advice and strategy:elink.
:li.:link reftype=hd res=008.Menus and keys:elink.
:li.:link reftype=hd res=009.About Caribbean Poker and license:elink.
:eul.
:p.

:h1 res=002.How to begin
:font facename=Helv size=8x12.
:p.
You need money to play. Choose :hp2.Cash - Add $100:ehp2. (or press :hp2.Add $100:ehp2.) to add money to the bank; :hp2.Cash Out:ehp2. takes it home. :hp2.Game - New Game:ehp2. sets the bank back to $100.
:p.
Set the ante ($5 to $100) in the spin field and press :hp2.Ante:ehp2. (key A). The bank must hold three times the ante, the ante itself and the bet which may follow, plus $1 if you play the progressive. Five cards are dealt to you and one to the dealer; the name of your hand is shown under your cards.
:p.
Then you decide&colon. :hp2.Bet:ehp2. (key B) puts twice the ante in the bet field, and the dealer's other cards are turned up; :hp2.Fold:ehp2. (key F) gives up the ante. The :hp2.Advice:ehp2. button (key V) suggests what to do.

:h1 res=003.Stud
:font facename=Helv size=8x12.
:p.
In the Stud variant nothing is exchanged. The dealer must have at least an Ace/King to open. If the dealer does not open, you get back the ante and the bet, plus a payment equal to the ante.
:p.
If the dealer opens, the hands are compared. If yours is higher you are paid the ante and the bet back, a payment equal to the ante, and the bet multiplied by the payout of your hand (see :link reftype=hd res=006.Payout table:elink.). If the dealer's hand is higher, the ante and the bet are lost. A tie returns the ante and the bet.

:h1 res=004.Draw
:font facename=Helv size=8x12.
:p.
In the Draw variant you may exchange up to two cards. After the deal, click the cards you want to throw away (up to two); they turn face down, and click them again to keep them. When you bet, the marked cards are replaced.
:p.
The dealer also draws, by a fixed strategy&colon. the dealer keeps made hands, throws away the odd card of two pair, the two other cards of three of a kind, the weakest cards of a pair, and draws to four card flushes and straights. To open, the dealer needs a pair of eights or better; otherwise you get back the ante and the bet, plus a payment equal to the ante. The payouts are lower than in Stud (see the payout table). Otherwise the rules are those of Stud.

:h1 res=005.Progressive jackpot
:font facename=Helv size=8x12.
:p.
Before the ante you may put a $1 chip in the progressive slot (:hp2.Progressive:ehp2. button, key P), or check :hp2.Auto:ehp2. to do it on every hand. The jackpot is paid for your first five cards, whether you bet, fold or win&colon. a flush pays $50, a full house $100, four of a kind $500, a straight flush 10 percent of the jackpot and a royal flush the whole jackpot. The chip is lost after the hand.
:p.
The jackpot grows all the time and never falls below $10,000.

:h1 res=006.Payout table
:font facename=Helv size=8x12.
:p.
The payout is a multiple of the bet (twice the ante), added to the return of the ante and the bet and to a payment equal to the ante.
:p.
:dl tsize=22 break=all.
:dt.:hp2.Royal Flush:ehp2.
:dd.Stud&colon. 100&colon.1   Draw&colon. 100&colon.1
:dt.:hp2.Straight Flush:ehp2.
:dd.Stud&colon. 50&colon.1   Draw&colon. 50&colon.1
:dt.:hp2.Four of a kind:ehp2.
:dd.Stud&colon. 25&colon.1   Draw&colon. 25&colon.1
